<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Glow Up — the app.

  Audited rather than copied (#132). Every required-reason family was searched
  for across both targets' sources; UserDefaults is the only one this app
  touches. File-timestamp, disk-space, system-boot-time, active-keyboard and
  pasteboard APIs return no matches, so none of them is declared here — a
  manifest that over-declares is as wrong as one that under-declares.

  Two reasons, and both are real in this binary:

    1C8F.1  The App Group's defaults. GlowSettings.store is
            UserDefaults(suiteName: "group.com.georgklock.glow"), and it is how
            the app and the widget extension share the glow level, the week
            preferences, the pop switch, the tap burst, the widget trace and
            WidgetKit's per-family display sizes.
            Read and written only within this app group.

    CA92.1  The app's own defaults. DailyHabitMigration records whether this
            install has been swept of per-day habits in UserDefaults.standard,
            the Low Power notice records that it has been shown, and
            GlowSettings falls back to .standard if the group container is ever
            unavailable.
            Read and written only by this app.

  NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is empty, and that is a statement about the
  product rather than an omission: nothing here is uploaded, synced or sent
  anywhere. History leaves the device only through the share sheet, on a tap,
  to wherever the person sending it chooses. There is no network code in either
  target — no URLSession, no Network framework.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>1C8F.1</string>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
